# Use python3

On this machine `python` is not the interpreter to use. Write `python3` in shell commands, docs, shebangs, and subprocess calls.

```bash
# Bad
python -m pytest
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt

# Good
python3 -m pytest
python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```

A virtualenv still applies. Activate `.venv`, then run `python3`.
